# Local development. On Zerops this comes from the platform: services are addressed by
# hostname on the project's private network (db:5432) and Zerops injects credentials as
# `servicehostname_ENVKEY` — you do not hand-manage them.
#
# This file previously also declared QDRANT_URL, NATS_URL and BRAIN_SCOPE, left over from an
# earlier design that was cut. Nothing in src/ ever read them. They were not harmless: the
# repo scanner reads .env, so Brain reported that its OWN repository needed Qdrant and NATS,
# and wrote both into the exported zerops.yaml. A tool whose entire claim is "here is what
# your repo actually needs" cannot be wrong about itself.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:brain@127.0.0.1:55432/brain

# Optional. Set this and the app skips the token gate — for development only; the UI never
# needs it and nothing persists a token to disk.
# ZEROPS_TOKEN=
